      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T09:24:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@mayank.metha@intel.com can you explain further?\n\nIf there is no type annotation, how is entity-manager supposed to know which type it should publish on D-Bus?\n\nA value like `8` can be represented by various types.\n\n`x-dbus-type` was specifically created to solve this issue.",
      "parentUuid": "8c85ff14_537c7978",
      "revId": "e5f6e51b72dfb1cbfa53dd6353750f05697f291c",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2bd53a2c_49a88eaa",
        "filename": "schemas/platform/mctp.json",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T09:47:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doesn\u0027t type field already handles this? Maybe im missing something here. Can you help highlight how `x-dbus-type` is different from `type`?",
      "parentUuid": "d87ad4a8_32f3b4b0",
      "revId": "e5f6e51b72dfb1cbfa53dd6353750f05697f291c",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c066addb_d153a20e",
        "filename": "schemas/platform/mctp.json",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002790
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T09:58:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`type` only describes the JSON value, so `integer` says nothing about width, and entity-manager publishes any JSON integer as a `t` by default. `x-dbus-type` says `StaticEid` is published as a `y`, the type an EID has in `mctpd`, which minimum and maximum only validate but don\u0027t change.",
      "parentUuid": "2bd53a2c_49a88eaa",
      "revId": "e5f6e51b72dfb1cbfa53dd6353750f05697f291c",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e82b7e6a_626700b5",
        "filename": "schemas/platform/mctp.json",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001712
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T09:58:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`type` field is defined by json-schema and used to validate configuration.\n\n`x-dbus-type` is loaded by entity-manager at runtime to know which type to publish on D-Bus.\n\nFor example if we have field `Address` it may be type `\"type\": \"string\"` and `\"x-dbus-type\": \"uint64\"`\n\nsuch that we can use template vars like `\"Address\": \"$bus + 1\"`\n\neven though the address is an unsigned integer at runtime.\n\nsee\nhttps://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-validation#name-type\n\nhttps://dbus.freedesktop.org/doc/dbus-specification.html#basic-types\n\nfor further information on this topic.",
      "parentUuid": "2bd53a2c_49a88eaa",
      "revId": "e5f6e51b72dfb1cbfa53dd6353750f05697f291c",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
